Everything is rebuilt with
make clean
make


For task A the code can be run manually as such:
make clean
make 
./main A

Task A tests the QR decomposition:
- A2 checks that a tall matrix A can be factorized as A = QR
- it checks that R is upper triangular
- it checks that Q^T Q is the identity
- A3 uses QR to solve Ax = b
- A4 computes the determinant from the QR decomposition

For task B the code can be run manually in the same way:
make clean 
make
./main B

Task B uses the QR decomposition to compute the inverse matrix A^{-1}.
It checks that A A^{-1} = I and A^{-1} A = I.

For task C it can be run as 
make clean
make
make out.times.data
gnuplot plot_C.gpi

The files Task_A.txt and Task_B.txt are the results of running ./main A and ./main B respectively. 

QR_runtime.svg is the result of task C. It is the runtime as function of N

Task C measures how long the QR decomposition takes for random NxN matrices.
The timing data is saved in out.times.data and plotted with plot_C.gpi.
The expected scaling is approximately O(N^3).

AI was used for the code. 


